---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContentCard from "../../components/ContentCard.astro";
import { experiments } from "../../data/content";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Product Image Lab Notes"
  description="Reproducible product-image tests covering browser format encoding, thumbnail crop geometry, and image memory estimates."
  activeNav="/experiments/"
>
  <section class="legal-hero legal-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">THE LAB</p>
    <h1>Small tests. Explicit limits.</h1>
    <p>
      Each note states the input, environment, method and result so a reader
      can reproduce it. A controlled fixture or geometry calculation can
      explain one behavior; it cannot predict every seller photo, browser or
      marketplace pipeline.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="shell page-section two-column-copy">
    <div>
      <h2>What is measured</h2>
      <p>
        The format test records the bytes produced from the same deterministic
        sample. The crop test calculates which centered pixels a frame removes.
        The memory note estimates one decoded RGBA buffer from pixel count.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>What the results do not prove</h2>
      <p>
        The format sample is not a photograph and its byte counts are not a
        universal format ranking. Geometry does not recreate an Etsy or Shopify
        theme. Memory arithmetic is not a device limit. Use the local tools to
        test your own files and inspect the actual destination preview.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="shell content-grid three-up page-section" aria-label="All lab notes">
    {experiments.map((item) => (
      <ContentCard
        eyebrow={item.category}
        title={item.title}
        description={item.description}
        href={`/experiments/${item.slug}/`}
        meta={`Rechecked ${item.lastVerified}`}
      />
    ))}
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
